From f040ace504a1308b44245e9c417b63b775028f65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Care Africa <dev@careafrica.local>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:56:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Practice modules: features follow the type of practice

- Migration 0006: plan, clinical_records (off/intake/full) and claims_enabled on practices;
  plan limits enforced in the database; only Care Africa can change a plan; existing
  free-text practice types mapped to the fixed list and modules backfilled
- Practice types (src/lib/practiceTypes.ts) in three groups with default modules;
  module rules and useModules hook (src/lib/modules.ts)
- Onboarding: new first step to choose the practice type, with a preview of what's
  included; finishing setup saves the recommended modules; medical aids only asked
  of clinical practices; header logo fixed
- Settings: Modules tab (core always on, clinical level, claims, plan locks,
  reset to recommended); practice type is now a fixed list
- Tests: 15 new database checks (82 in total)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
